<title>MEXICO: Mexican daily port, shipping update for July 22.</title>
<headline>Mexican daily port, shipping update for July 22.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>All Mexican ports were open to shipping on Tuesday, the Communications and Transport Ministry (SCT) said in its 1000 local/1500 GMT daily meteorological report.</p>
<p>Tropical storms in the region took a break in the beginning of hurricane season. Tropical depression Danny caused some isolated rains along the Campeche coast in the Gulf of Mexico.</p>
<p>Rains were expected in the afternoon across the country, with electric storms forecast along the Pacific coast and in the Gulf of Tehuantepec.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
